  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Liberia: Strengthening Gender Equality in Law Enforcement Agencies in Liberia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Targeted women security officers have the knowledge required to improve their                professional skills and chances for promotion. 2) LIFLEA coordinates the promotion of gender equality in                security sector agencies in close coordination with ancillary women associations. 3) Leadership of                security agencies are aware of the need for a greater role for the gender sections in investigating                complaints of gender discrimination.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Female security officers including officers from the Liberia                National Police, Liberia Immigration Service, Liberia Drug Enforcement Agency, Monrovia City Police,                Executive Protection Service, the Bureau of Correction and Rehabilitation and the Liberia National Fire                Service; associations of female security agencies and LIFLEA; and gender and human rights units of                security agencies. Indirect beneficiaries: Security sector agencies and the Liberia population.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to ensure that women in the security sector apply the knowledge                acquired and use the advocacy platforms and internal control mechanisms of the Liberia Female Law                Enforcement Agency (LIFLEA) to protect their rights and advance their careers.</narrative>
  </description>
